  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463314",
      "title": "Project Setup & First Methods",
      "lectureOrder": 53,
      "videoOrder": 47,
      "sourceHash": "2d175218539841bc1a3a4e12a6ffa66a2870554d48ae7f95ea8c936152b7fd34",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.29,
          "end": 3.66,
          "en": "So let's get started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.66,
          "end": 7.33,
          "en": "Attached to this lecture, you find this starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.33,
          "end": 12.04,
          "en": "which is this index HTML file with a basic skeleton",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.04,
          "end": 13.72,
          "en": "for our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.72,
          "end": 18.28,
          "en": "No Vue logic is in there yet, it's really just HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.28,
          "end": 21.07,
          "en": "You got to style CSS file with some basic styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.07,
          "end": 22.91,
          "en": "we're going to use throughout this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.91,
          "end": 24.66,
          "en": "so throughout this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.66,
          "end": 27.91,
          "en": "And you've got an empty app JS file because we're going to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.91,
          "end": 31.163,
          "en": "write all the Vue logic together step by step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.63,
          "end": 34.68,
          "en": "Now, as I said in the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.68,
          "end": 37.81,
          "en": "we're going to build a simple monster slayer game",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.81,
          "end": 40.8,
          "en": "where we have a monster health and our health.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.8,
          "end": 43.66,
          "en": "We've got various options for attacking,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.66,
          "end": 45.24,
          "en": "launching a special attack,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.24,
          "end": 47.26,
          "en": "healing ourselves or surrendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.26,
          "end": 50.36,
          "en": "and we wanna implement all of that with Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.36,
          "end": 53.86,
          "en": "so that we have this browser based game here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.86,
          "end": 56.72,
          "en": "which we can fully control with JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.72,
          "end": 59.85,
          "en": "but of course not with just JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.85,
          "end": 63.66,
          "en": "but instead with Vue and JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.66,
          "end": 67.07,
          "en": "And for that, obviously we're going to start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.07,
          "end": 69.98,
          "en": "by controlling this with Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.98,
          "end": 74.76,
          "en": "So by taking over control over some HTML code with Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.76,
          "end": 77.74,
          "en": "so that we can use Vue features here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.74,
          "end": 80.94,
          "en": "And you might notice I already prepared this div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.94,
          "end": 85.41,
          "en": "with an ID game here and well, that looks very tempting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.41,
          "end": 87.08,
          "en": "And indeed this is the div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.08,
          "end": 89.06,
          "en": "we're going to control with the Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.06,
          "end": 92.45,
          "en": "because it turns out that inside of that div,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.45,
          "end": 95.59,
          "en": "we got the entire game HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.59,
          "end": 97.85,
          "en": "The header is outside of the div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.85,
          "end": 101.33,
          "en": "but the header is nothing we need to control with Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.33,
          "end": 104.84,
          "en": "We're not going to use any Vue features in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.84,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "Therefore in app JS, like we did many times before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "we can create a Vue app by calling Vue.createApp",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 115.35,
          "en": "and we can store it as a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.35,
          "end": 120.35,
          "en": "and then mount our app here to this game div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.46,
          "end": 123.65,
          "en": "So to this div with an ID game and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.65,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "we use the ID game selector here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 130.3,
          "en": "So now we got a Vue app connected to this div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.3,
          "end": 134.423,
          "en": "and now the question is with which parts do we wanna start?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.26,
          "end": 138.46,
          "en": "There certainly is not just one possible route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.46,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "you could take, there are multiple routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 142.96,
          "en": "like always in programming,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.96,
          "end": 145.03,
          "en": "but I would suggest that we simply start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.03,
          "end": 146.82999999999998,
          "en": "with the attack button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.82999999999998,
          "end": 150.2,
          "en": "So we basically implement features top to bottom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.2,
          "end": 154.19,
          "en": "So the attack button here when pressed should of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.19,
          "end": 157.6,
          "en": "reduce the Monster's health, but at the same time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.6,
          "end": 160.03,
          "en": "the monster should then also strike back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.03,
          "end": 162.79,
          "en": "so that our health is also reduced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.79,
          "end": 167.79,
          "en": "And we probably don't want to use a single hard-coded value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.07999999999998,
          "end": 170.03,
          "en": "by which we reduce healths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.03,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "but we wanna use some randomness",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 175.21,
          "en": "so that our game isn't too predictable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.21,
          "end": 177.71,
          "en": "And therefore in app JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.71,
          "end": 180.87,
          "en": "I'm going to start by managing some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.87,
          "end": 184.55,
          "en": "And you already saw it by now in the last lectures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.55,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "and modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 190.52,
          "en": "data of course is a core concept, a core thing in Vue apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.07,
          "end": 194.26,
          "en": "because pretty much any app you're going to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.26,
          "end": 195.95,
          "en": "needs some data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.95,
          "end": 198.05,
          "en": "no matter what you're managing in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.05,
          "end": 200.79,
          "en": "but you're going to need some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.79,
          "end": 203.11,
          "en": "Think of data as the variables you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.11,
          "end": 205.87,
          "en": "in your regular JavaScript codes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.87,
          "end": 208.95,
          "en": "and it makes a lot of sense that we need data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.95,
          "end": 210.96,
          "en": "For example, here in this game,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.96,
          "end": 213.94,
          "en": "which kind of data do we need to manage here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.94,
          "end": 217.67000000000002,
          "en": "to make anything really work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.67000000000002,
          "end": 221.85,
          "en": "Well, how about the healths of the player and the monster?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.85,
          "end": 224,
          "en": "We need to manage that data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224,
          "end": 226.38,
          "en": "we need to manage that health data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.38,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "because we're going to change it and changes in the health",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 234.27,
          "en": "of course, should later be reflected back on the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 234.27,
          "end": 237.57999999999998,
          "en": "so that these health bars are reduced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.57999999999998,
          "end": 240.82,
          "en": "So therefore we need data, we need this data option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 240.82,
          "end": 243.55,
          "en": "in our Vue app configuration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.55,
          "end": 247.52,
          "en": "And as you learnt in this data method which it should be,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.52,
          "end": 251.55,
          "en": "we returned the object that holds our actual data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.55,
          "end": 256.54,
          "en": "And here as I just explained, I have two main data points",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.54,
          "end": 258.87,
          "en": "and that would be the player health.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 258.87,
          "end": 262.38,
          "en": "And let's say we start at a value of 100 here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 262.38,
          "end": 265.83,
          "en": "though of course you can pick any values you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.83,
          "end": 268.14,
          "en": "and we'll need a monster health.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 268.14,
          "end": 271.44,
          "en": "Now we could say to monster has more or less health,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 271.44,
          "end": 274.363,
          "en": "but I'm always going to set the monster health to 100.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 275.52,
          "end": 279.89,
          "en": "So now we got these two health values which allow us to well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.89,
          "end": 284.62,
          "en": "manage the health of our two game participants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.62,
          "end": 286.83,
          "en": "But the health alone is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 286.83,
          "end": 289.58,
          "en": "Of course, we also need ways of changing the health,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.58,
          "end": 292.28,
          "en": "for example, when an attack is launched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 292.28,
          "end": 297.12,
          "en": "So that screams for methods because methods are essentially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.12,
          "end": 301.27,
          "en": "the actions we support in our Vue application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.27,
          "end": 304.12,
          "en": "For example, when the attack button is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 304.12,
          "end": 308.65,
          "en": "we want to trigger a method that reduces the monster health.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.65,
          "end": 312.94,
          "en": "And therefore I'm going to name that method attackMonster,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 312.94,
          "end": 314.26,
          "en": "because that's what we're doing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 314.26,
          "end": 316.373,
          "en": "We're attacking the monster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.6,
          "end": 320.33,
          "en": "Now, what should we do inside of this method then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.33,
          "end": 323.525,
          "en": "What should happen instead of attackMonster?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 323.525,
          "end": 327.29,
          "en": "Well, we wanna calculate the damage we're dealing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 327.29,
          "end": 329.5,
          "en": "and we then want to reduce the monster health",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 329.5,
          "end": 331.29,
          "en": "by that damage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 331.29,
          "end": 335.52,
          "en": "And as I said before, I wanna use a random value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.52,
          "end": 338.69,
          "en": "You could, of course always deduct the same amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.69,
          "end": 340.08,
          "en": "from the monster health",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.08,
          "end": 343.15,
          "en": "but your game would be pretty predictable then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 343.15,
          "end": 345.49,
          "en": "So to calculate a random value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 345.49,
          "end": 348.31,
          "en": "we can use the math random function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 348.31,
          "end": 351.78,
          "en": "which gives us a random number between zero and one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 351.78,
          "end": 354.96,
          "en": "Now, I don't want a value between zero and one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 354.96,
          "end": 358.48,
          "en": "Instead, since we're working with a health of 100,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 358.48,
          "end": 360.98,
          "en": "we probably want a higher number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 360.98,
          "end": 365.31,
          "en": "So for example, we could say that we want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 365.31,
          "end": 369.09,
          "en": "get a random number between a minimum and the maximum value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 369.09,
          "end": 371.5,
          "en": "Let's say between five and 12,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 371.5,
          "end": 374.22,
          "en": "we wanna deal at least five points of damage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 374.22,
          "end": 377.36,
          "en": "but no more than 12 points of damage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 377.36,
          "end": 380.7,
          "en": "And the formula for calculating this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 380.7,
          "end": 384.36,
          "en": "is to multiply math random",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 384.36,
          "end": 388.77,
          "en": "with the difference of max, which is 12 as I just explained",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 388.77,
          "end": 393.25,
          "en": "minus the min value, which should be five, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 393.25,
          "end": 398.25,
          "en": "And then we take the floor of that to round it down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 398.31,
          "end": 401.65999999999997,
          "en": "so that we don't have a number with a decimal place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 401.65999999999997,
          "end": 403.7,
          "en": "but we have an integer number instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 403.7,
          "end": 406.13,
          "en": "and we add the minimum again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 406.13,
          "end": 409.5,
          "en": "This is a formula for calculating a random number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 409.5,
          "end": 411.14300000000003,
          "en": "between five and 12.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 412.53,
          "end": 417.53,
          "en": "So this will give me my attack value let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 418.7,
          "end": 420.963,
          "en": "by which I wanna reduce to monster health.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 424.53,
          "end": 426.66,
